   "source": [
    "# SpamJam: data exploration\n",
    "\n",
    "SpamJam helps GrandPied's IT team flag spam (`is_spam` = 1) while protecting legitimate emails (`is_spam` = 0). The problem and the cost of each mistake are described in the README and used in `analysis.ipynb` to choose our metric and threshold.\n",
    "\n",
    "We load the Spambase dataset (UCI, id 94) through our package. The first run downloads it and saves it, and then later runs read that file. We then remove duplicates, split the data into a training and a test set, and explore the training set only."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "f163471a55d3587",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-10-27T15:06:15.726481Z",
     "start_time": "2026-10-27T15:06:15.698894Z"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from spamjam.data import DatasetLoader\n",
    "import logging\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import yaml\n",
    "import joblib\n",
    "from spamjam import constants\n",
    "\n",
    "logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO)\n",
    "pd.set_option(\"display.max_columns\", None)\n",
    "\n",
    "#loading\n",
    "loader = DatasetLoader.from_config()\n",
    "df = loader.load_data()\n",
    "\n",
    "df.shape"
   ],
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
