  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "70002842",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "About 39% of emails are spam. The classes do not have the same amount of data so we have to ensure that when separating the data into the train and test sets we use stratify to ensure that the same proportion of the different classes exist in both the train and test sets."
   ]
  },
  {
   "metadata": {},
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "source": "## **Saving processed train and test datasets**",
   "id": "b5e3cb5d6757ab03"
  },
  {
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-10-27T15:06:16.021267Z",
     "start_time": "2026-10-27T15:06:16.012867Z"
    }
   },
   "cell_type": "code",
   "source": [
    "#Load config\n",
    "with open(constants.CONFIG_PATH, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
    "    config = yaml.safe_load(f)\n",
    "\n",
    "#Get paths from config\n",
    "processed_dir = constants.PROJECT_ROOT / config[\"data\"][\"processed_dir\"]\n",
    "processed_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "train_filename = config[\"data\"][\"train_filename\"]\n",
    "test_filename = config[\"data\"][\"test_filename\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "#Save the dataframes\n",
    "joblib.dump(train_df, processed_dir / train_filename)\n",
    "joblib.dump(test_df, processed_dir / test_filename)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\" Train and Test sets saved in {processed_dir}\")"
   ],
